    description: "Since PR #1504 (WI-bapal), `vendor/` is no longer excluded by name, so committed vendored code is analysed as tier 3 (intended). On hypergumbo's own repo that pulls in the committed tree-sitter grammars under vendor/, including generated parser.c files (~10 MB each); self-survey went 3:54 → 4:55 wall and 2.95 → 3.35 GB peak RSS (+221 symbols, +313 edges, all tier 3). tree-sitter-generated parser.c / scanner tables are machine output: classify them as tier 4 (derived) via GENERATED_CODE_PATTERNS / the derived header check (tree-sitter emits a recognisable header and `#include \"tree_sitter/parser.h\"` + huge static tables) so they're skipped like other generated code. Check analogues: other generators that commit large C/Go tables (bison/yacc *.tab.c, re2c, protobuf .pb.c, ragel). Measure self-survey before/after."  # b7f2
    fields: {}  # b7f2
